Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 15:30:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] Publish the checkout minus the workshop, then e2e the
 live site
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

GitHub Pages used to serve the whole branch, so src/, the tests, the notes
and the tooling were all online. Now, on every push to master once
`verify` passed (so the decks online are the ones `make check` proved
built from src/):

- `pages` removes src/, the Makefile, README, TODO, LICENSE and the
  dotfiles from the checkout and deploys the rest with the Pages actions
  (.git / .github are never uploaded). No staging directory, no list of
  what the site is: the site is the root minus the workshop.
  One-time setup on the repo: Settings → Pages → Source: GitHub Actions
- `pages-check` runs the deck e2e tests against the site just deployed:
  E2E_BASE=<page_url> makes decks.test.js skip its own server, count that
  base as local, and first fetch every live deck and compare it to the
  built slides/ file, retrying while the deploy propagates — so a green
  run says the live decks are byte-for-byte the built ones AND load
  without errors from the live URL. `E2E_BASE=… make test-live` locally.
  The narration tests stay local only (they need the test-only routes)
- the Chromium install / cache steps move to a composite action
  (.github/actions/chromium) used by both jobs

