+## Publishing
+GitHub Pages gets the checkout minus the workshop: on every push to
+`master`, once `verify` passed, the `pages` job of
+[verify.yml](.github/workflows/verify.yml) removes `src/`, the Makefile,
+README, TODO, LICENSE and the dotfiles from the checkout and deploys the rest
+(`.git` / `.github` are never uploaded) — so what is online is exactly what
+`make check` proved built from `src/`. Then `pages-check` runs the deck e2e
+tests against the live site (`E2E_BASE=https://…/ make test-live`): it waits
+until every live deck is byte-for-byte the built `slides/` file, then opens
+each one from the live URL with the same checks as locally. One-time setup on
+the repo: Settings → Pages → Build and deployment → Source: **GitHub
+Actions**.
